# The constructed fixed exceptional pair and its matter action

The finite exceptional coordinates construct an actual irreducible root
pairing, a simple 248-dimensional matrix Lie algebra, and its compact real
form. An explicit adjoint identification realizes the order-three grading
as an actual 86-dimensional subalgebra and two 81-dimensional modules.

Explicit commuting classical matrix units embed the actual Standard Model
and family algebra. A signed basis map identifies its action on one actual
exceptional half with the previously constructed matter representation.
The full restricted cubic-radical and local anomaly identities therefore
hold for that actual exceptional subspace. Its action under the entire
degree-zero algebra is irreducible. The full zero-grade cubic radical is
the explicit 78-dimensional span of six coroots and 72 root vectors.

Compact conjugation constructs the actual 86-dimensional compact isotropy
and its entire 162-dimensional real orthogonal complement. A polynomial
in one family generator recovers the complex structure and proves that
the complement's full real commutant is `ℂ`. Transport to the canonical
Hermitian half proves its full cubic radical is nonzero. Thus the actual
fixed pair satisfies the original algebraic hypotheses.

The full radical is Lie-isomorphic to the simple E₆ root-lattice algebra.
The local 27 is irreducible with first fundamental highest weight. The two
factors are mutual centralizers. The compact radical has real dimension 78
and is simple. The real isotropy splits as its product with the standard
special unitary Lie algebra on three complex coordinates.
Exceptional group integration and global uniqueness remain open.
